Spec: Publisher device and service authority

Purpose:
  Persist device trust and least-scope service grants that the actual publishing Agent enforces.

Owns:
  ./SecureAuthority.cs

References:
  ./RegistrationReview.sdd
  ./JournalCapacity.sdd
  ./SecureIdentity.sdd

Must:
  Include exact local visitor grants in schema validation and reserved revocation accounting; peer revocation atomically retires both publisher and visitor authority.
  Bind grants to authenticated device key, client application, reviewed publisher application and fixed export service.
  Reserve logical revoke capacity for every active device/grant and retain administrator operation outcomes atomically.
  Use monotonic revisions and compare reviewed proposals before activation; re-trust or re-grant never revives old authority.
  Bind live grants to authority epochs rather than denial-only review counters; approval proposals still bind the complete review decision version.
  Reject new opens immediately after committed revocation and expose revocation state to active-session monitoring.
  Never accept ordinary application grant approval or caller-supplied target addresses.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Verify exact scope, versioned approval, retained decisions and grant/device revocation in the direct preview.
